     Blessing (or cursing) corpses does not alter the period
of time until they rot away.  It only affects how long they
remain safely edible before giving the "that was tainted"
fatal poisoning effect; they still rot away at exactly the
same rate as an ordinary uncursed corpse.  The duration that
a corpse lasts is determined via the infamous rnz() function
(also used for prayer timeout) which typically produces a
very substantial random variation.


